<title>SOUTH KOREA: Korea wheat imports from U.S. up 6.6 pct in 1996.</title>
<headline>Korea wheat imports from U.S. up 6.6 pct in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's wheat imports from the United States rose 6.6 percent to 1.61 million tonnes in 1996 from 1.51 tonnes in 1995, an official with the Korea International Trade Association (KITA) said on Friday.</p>
<p>Australian wheat imports reached 725,987 tonnes in 1996, compared to 640,565 tonnes in 1995, the official said.</p>
<p>Wheat imports from Canada also jumped to 528,764 tonnes last year from 189,795 tonnes the previous year.</p>
<p>The country's total wheat imports in 1996 rose to 3.18 million tonnes from 2.34 million tonnes in 1995.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
</text>
